# Implementation Prompt — Lightning Network Nodes Backend Challenge

## 1. Role and Objective

Act as a **Senior/Staff Rust Backend Engineer**, specializing in distributed systems, database performance, system design, concurrency, reliability, and clean software architecture.

Implement a complete, production-quality backend application in Rust based on the **Superhuman Back-end Coding Challenge**.

Your responsibility is to design, implement, test, document, and validate the entire application.

**Do not deliver pseudocode, incomplete implementations, placeholder functions, or illustrative snippets. Implement working code and execute the available tests and quality checks.**

Use pragmatic engineering. Prefer correctness, maintainability, performance, and simplicity over unnecessary abstractions or infrastructure complexity.

The application must:

1. Fetch Lightning Network nodes from the mempool.space API.
2. Persist the data in PostgreSQL.
3. Maintain a history of successful imports using immutable snapshots.
4. Always serve the latest successfully published snapshot.
5. Keep serving the previous snapshot if an import fails.
6. Synchronize automatically every 10 minutes by default.
7. Allow the synchronization interval to be configured.
8. Expose `GET /nodes` with the required transformations.
9. Include the timestamp indicating when the imported data was saved.
10. Provide efficient PostgreSQL reads and bulk writes.
11. Include comprehensive unit and integration tests.
12. Provide Docker and Docker Compose configurations.
13. Manage development tools using mise.
14. Manage development commands using a justfile.
15. Include SQL migrations.
16. Provide a collection of executable HTTP requests.
17. Include comprehensive documentation and a reproducible developer workflow.

The result must be a complete Git repository ready for review.

