## 24. Acceptance Criteria

The implementation is complete only when the following conditions are satisfied.

### Functional

- [ ] The application is implemented entirely in Rust.
- [ ] PostgreSQL persists all successfully imported snapshots.
- [ ] The application imports data from mempool.space.
- [ ] Synchronization runs every 600 seconds by default.
- [ ] The interval can be overridden by TOML or environment variable.
- [ ] Synchronization runs on startup without blocking HTTP availability.
- [ ] The latest successful snapshot is the only one exposed by `GET /nodes`.
- [ ] Previous successful snapshots remain available as history.
- [ ] A failed synchronization does not remove or replace valid data.
- [ ] `GET /nodes` works while the external API is unavailable.
- [ ] Monetary values are converted precisely.
- [ ] Dates are formatted correctly in UTC.
- [ ] `saved_at` is returned in extended mode.
- [ ] Original four-field compatibility mode works.
- [ ] Snapshot publication is atomic.

### Performance

- [ ] Database queries are parameterized.
- [ ] The read query uses appropriate indexes.
- [ ] No N+1 queries exist.
- [ ] Inserts are batched.
- [ ] Database pools are configurable.
- [ ] Read and write paths are separated logically.
- [ ] Benchmark tooling is included.
- [ ] No unsubstantiated latency claims are made.

### Infrastructure

- [ ] PostgreSQL migrations work on an empty database.
- [ ] Dockerfile builds the application.
- [ ] Docker Compose starts PostgreSQL and the application.
- [ ] mise installs/configures the required development tools.
- [ ] The justfile provides the documented commands.
- [ ] The HTTP request collection works.
- [ ] `.env.example` documents required configuration.
- [ ] No secrets are hardcoded into production defaults.

### Quality

- [ ] Unit tests pass.
- [ ] Integration tests pass.
- [ ] Concurrency tests pass.
- [ ] `cargo fmt --check` passes.
- [ ] `cargo clippy -- -D warnings` passes.
- [ ] Release build succeeds.
- [ ] README contains reproducible instructions.
- [ ] The project includes no placeholder implementations.

